    {
      "id": 90,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        920,
        760
      ],
      "size": [
        560,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 32,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## LTX-2.5 V2V · First/Last frame · IC-LoRA · Tiled Fusion\n\n1. **Source video** → drives the IC-LoRA (control / structure).\n2. **FIRST frame** and **LAST frame** images → pinned at frame 0 and the final frame.\n3. **PROMPT** → describe look, lighting, motion and grade.\n4. Set **width/height** (multiples of 32) and **length** (8n+1: 97, 121 …).\n\n**Tiled Fusion rules (from Lightricks' docs):**\n- Sampler must be `euler` / `heun` / `dpm_2` (no ancestral, no dpmpp_2m).\n- Keep `overlap_frac` ≥ 0.5; tile size = the IC-LoRA's trained window (1024×576 default).\n- IC-LoRA guide: `use_tiled_encode` **false**, `latent_downscale_factor` **1**.\n  IC-LoRAs trained at a reduced reference (e.g. *union-control ref0.5*) are **not** supported by Tiled Fusion.\n- `tile_frames` stays **0** (whole clip in one pass). Temporal streaming pairs one guide per\n  window and would break the first/last-frame guides.\n- No LTXVCropGuides needed: the sampler drops the appended guide frames itself.\n\nGuide strength 0.7 matches the official FLF2V template; raise to 1.0 to lock the exact pixels.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
